{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Is it not et that, etc.; I will watch, etc.</b> Meaning: not as you think, that there is no obligation upon me when the speech comes from HaShem to bless, and I could muzzle my mouth and not speak — not so; rather, he is forbidden to hold it back. And therefore the verse is precise in the language of watching, after the manner of our Sages of blessed memory (Shevuot 36a): every instance of השמר (take heed), פן (lest), and אל (do not) is nothing but a negative prohibition, so that he is warned not to fall silent, and if he transgresses he is liable to death. And without the expression אשמר (I will watch) it would not have been heard, and from this it follows that he is under compulsion. And our Sages of blessed memory (Numbers Rabbah ch. 20) said that He said to him: would that he had died rather than bless Israel — see, everything he blessed was under compulsion and not from his own heart." "<b>Further,</b> it intends according to the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Yalkut Shimoni), that a plate of iron stood in his mouth: if he wished to curse, it would prevent him; to bless — he could; and that is the meaning of <b>et it I will watch</b> — so that I might be able to speak, for without this he would have been silenced." "Or it is possible that he intended to tell him that he hopes and looks forward to HaShem putting His word in his mouth to speak, and that is the meaning of <b>that HaShem will put in my mouth — et it I will watch</b>, meaning he hopes and looks forward to speaking, for he tastes a great taste that neither he nor all the families of the nations are worthy of, as is known — how sweet to the soul is the taste of the holy power whose word is upon one's tongue. And even though HaShem put something in his mouth, and we explained that this was so the words would not touch a pig's mouth, even so he tastes a taste and it is sweet to him."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:13:12.114379055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}